    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently test the body parts of Lord Shiva worshipped at each Panch Kedar site (e.g., Hump at Kedarnath, Arms at Tungnath, Face at Rudranath, Belly/Navel at Madhyamaheshwar, Hair/Matted Locks at Kalpeshwar).",
        "Distinguish clearly between the Chota Char Dham circuit of Uttarakhand and the main All-India Char Dham circuit established by Adi Shankaracharya (Badrinath, Dwarka, Puri, Rameswaram).",
        "Remember the district locations of key pilgrimage sites: Badrinath and Kedarnath are located in Chamoli and Rudraprayag districts respectively."
      ],
      "id": "zrux2ql"
    },
